      "writtenOn": "2020-05-26T06:48:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe not.\n\nIf the board has a dumb battery (e.g. kukui), virtual_battery module has no knowledge about how to access it directly.\n\nIf the board has a smart battery, it\u0027s possible to access the battery. But without the knowledge about the meaning of the command, we don\u0027t know which kind of read we should use: sb_read, sb_read_string, or even read8 / read32.\n\nYes we can guess from read_len parameter, but I think it\u0027s not a good solution.",
      "parentUuid": "9d761216_19d9e855",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 307,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 307,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "a0cb0862ddcb31b8479c32d3f2169d0e9693d41c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
